hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27839","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Umm Atiyyah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us while we were washing his daughter, and he said: Wash her three times, or five, or more than that if you see fit, and put camphor in the last, or something of camphor, and when you finish then inform me. So we informed him, and he threw to us his waist wrapper and said: Wrap her in it."
"27840","Muhammad said: And Hafsah narrated it to us, she said: So we made her head into three braids."
"27841","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: When this verse was revealed, that they will not associate anything with Allah, up to His saying, nor disobey you in what is right, she said: Wailing was included in it. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, except the family of so-and-so, for they helped me wail in the pre-Islamic period, so I must help them wail. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Except the family of so-and-so."
"27842","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: One of the daughters of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and said: Wash her with lote leaves, and wash her an odd number, three or five or more than that if you see fit, and put camphor in the last, or something of camphor, and when you finish then inform me. She said: When we finished we informed him, upon him be prayer and peace, and he threw to us his waist wrapper and said: Wrap her in it."
"27843","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: I went on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seven expeditions, treating the sick and attending to their wounds, staying behind with them in their dwellings, preparing food for them."
"27844","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Khalid, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to me a sheep of charity, so I sent to A'ishah some of it. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to A'ishah, he said: Do you have anything? She said: No, except that Nusaybah sent to us of the sheep which you sent to her. So he said: It has reached its lawful place."
"27845","Isma'il narrated to us, from Khalid, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them concerning washing his daughter: Begin with her right side and the places of ablution on her."
"27846","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: We were forbidden from following funeral processions, but it was not made binding upon us."
"27847","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman shall not mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except a wife, for she mourns over her husband four months and ten days. She shall not wear a dyed garment except a garment of coarse striped cloth, nor apply kohl, nor perfume herself, except at the end of her purity a small portion of costus and nails."
"27848","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: He meant the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took pledge from us in the oath of allegiance that we would not wail. So no woman among us kept it except five: Umm Sulaym, the wife of Mu'adh, the daughter of Abi Sabrah, and another woman."
"27849","Yahya ibn Sa'id and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, she said: Umm Atiyyah narrated to me, she said: One of the daughters of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and said: Wash her with lote leaves, and wash her an odd number, three or five or more than that if you see that, and put camphor in the last, or something of camphor, and when you finish then inform me. She said: When we finished we informed him, and he threw to us his waist wrapper and said: Wrap her in it. Umm Atiyyah said: And we braided the head of the daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, into three braids, and we threw behind her her two side locks and her forelock."
"27850","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: We pledged allegiance to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he took upon us among what he took that we would not wail. An Ansari woman said: The family of so-and-so helped me wail in the pre-Islamic period, and among them is a mourning gathering, so I will not pledge to you until I help them wail as they helped me wail. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, agreed with her on that. So she went and helped them wail, then returned and pledged allegiance to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: Umm Atiyyah said: So no woman among us kept it except her and except Umm Sulaym bint Milhan."
"27851","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham and Habib informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took from the women among what he took that they would not wail. A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman helped me wail, shall I not help her wail? So she withheld her hand, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, withheld his hand, and he did not pledge her."
"27852","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq Abu Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Isma'il Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from his grandmother Umm Atiyyah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, he gathered the Ansari women in a house, then he sent to them Umar ibn al-Khattab. He stood at the door and greeted them, and they returned the greeting. He said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to you. They said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his messenger. He said: Pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill your children, nor bring a slander which you fabricate between your hands and feet, nor disobey in what is right. They said: Yes. So Umar extended his hand from outside the door, and they extended their hands from inside. Then he said: O Allah, bear witness. And he commanded us to bring out on the two Eids the secluded maidens and menstruating women, and we were forbidden from following funeral processions, and there is no Friday prayer upon us. So I asked him about slander and about His saying, nor disobey you in what is right. He said: It is wailing."
